\section{Conclusion}\label{sec:conclusion}

We tested whether SDF supervision and collision-aware evaluation deliver reliable geometric safety for VLAs. Action collapse renders reported CAR illusory; dfCAR corrects this using only EE position logging (\S\ref{sec:dfcar}). EE-only oracle SDF refinement is counterproductive, reducing CAR by 5--10\,pp as unmonitored links rotate through obstacles (\S\ref{sec:ee_only}), and collision-free demonstrations account for nearly all avoidance gains with no statistically significant SDF benefit (\S\ref{sec:avoidance_source}).

These findings carry two broader implications. First, dfCAR provides a lightweight diagnostic that any VLA evaluation pipeline can adopt to screen for action-collapse contamination. Second, point-supervision of a single link is insufficient for articulated robots; genuine geometric safety will require full-body collision representations and cross-architecture validation.
